/Title (price in reports of a draft de-escalation arrangement around the Strait of Hormuz. But the physical market has not caught up with the financial one. Hormuz tanker traffic remains stalled near a two-month low despite the reported peace signals, Ukraine's maritime drone campaign has cut dirty tanker loadings from Russian Black Sea and Sea of Azov ports by 62% in the last two weeks of July, and UN trade data shows Hormuz-dependent economies still running at roughly half their normal export volumes. For Southeast Asian operators, falling headline crude prices should not be read as a falling risk premium. Screening, war-risk allocation and route documentation remain conditions precedent on any Gulf, Red Sea or Black Sea-linked fixture.)
