/Title (Commercial Effect on Shipping A fast, large downward move in crude and bunker costs improves voyage economics and working-capital requirements in the near term, but it should not be read as a signal to loosen war-risk, insurance or routing terms in charter-parties. Owners and charterers fixing into the Gulf, Red Sea or Black Sea this week should treat the current price relief as provisional until the reported Hormuz arrangement is confirmed and reflected in actual transit volumes and underwriting terms.)
